chx:X_SignedTransactionHidesKey a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SignedTransactionHidesKey ; rdfs:label "a 222-byte payment with a key and no secret"@en ; skos:definition "A signed transaction contains the signature and the public key and never the private key: on the test chain the spending input had two witness items of 71 and 33 bytes, the 33 bytes were the public key, the 32-byte private key and its WIF text were not in the 222 bytes of the transaction, and the book's sentence is that a transaction authorizes only a specific value to a specific recipient and cannot be forged."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_SignedTransactionHidesKey a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b1_secrecy']; (s['n_witness_items'], s['witness_item_lengths'], s['pubkey_in_witness'], s['private_key_hex_in_tx'], s['wif_in_tx'], s['tx_bytes'], L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'A Bitcoin transaction authorizes only a specific value to a specific recipient and cannot be forged')) evaluates to (2, [71, 33], True, False, False, 222, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b1_secrecy']; (s['n_witness_items'], s['witness_item_lengths'], s['pubkey_in_witness'], s['private_key_hex_in_tx'], s['wif_in_tx'], s['tx_bytes'], L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'A Bitcoin transaction authorizes only a specific value to a specific recipient and cannot be forged'))" ; chx:output "(2, [71, 33], True, False, False, 222, True)" .
chx:X_SignedTransactionHidesKey rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SignedTransactionHidesKey .
chx:X_TamperBreaksSignature a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TamperBreaksSignature ; rdfs:label "an address swapped on the way"@en ; skos:definition "A signature covers the outputs, so a thief who changes them invalidates it: the valid transaction was accepted by testmempoolaccept, the same transaction with the recipient's script replaced by an attacker's script, and the same transaction with its first output lowered from 1.5 to 1 coin, were each refused with mempool-script-verify-flag-failed, the script failure that follows from the hashOutputs commitment of BIP 143."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_TamperBreaksSignature a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = R['b1_tamper']; (t['valid']['allowed'], t['address_replaced']['allowed'], t['address_replaced']['reject-reason'], t['amount_changed']['allowed'], t['amount_changed']['reject-reason'], t['address_replaced_differs'], t['amount_changed_differs'], L.has('bip-0143.mediawiki', 'hashOutputs')) evaluates to (True, False, 'mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Signature must be zero for failed CHECK(MULTI)SIG operation)', False, 'mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Signature must be zero for failed CHECK(MULTI)SIG operation)', True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); t = R['b1_tamper']; (t['valid']['allowed'], t['address_replaced']['allowed'], t['address_replaced']['reject-reason'], t['amount_changed']['allowed'], t['amount_changed']['reject-reason'], t['address_replaced_differs'], t['amount_changed_differs'], L.has('bip-0143.mediawiki', 'hashOutputs'))" ; chx:output "(True, False, 'mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Signature must be zero for failed CHECK(MULTI)SIG operation)', False, 'mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Signature must be zero for failed CHECK(MULTI)SIG operation)', True, True, True)" .
chx:X_TamperBreaksSignature rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TamperBreaksSignature .
chx:X_SighashAllIsTheDefault a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SighashAllIsTheDefault ; rdfs:label "the byte 01 at the end of the signature"@en ; skos:definition "The promise that a signed payment cannot be changed holds for the default signature type: the wallet's signature ended with the byte 01, SIGHASH_ALL, which commits to every output, while the interpreter of Bitcoin Core 31.1 also knows NONE, SINGLE and ANYONECANPAY, and BIP 143 says that hashOutputs commits to all outputs only when the type is neither SINGLE nor NONE."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_SighashAllIsTheDefault a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b1_secrecy']['sighash_byte'], L.has('core_src_script_interpreter.cpp', 'SIGHASH_NONE', 'SIGHASH_SINGLE', 'SIGHASH_ANYONECANPAY'), L.has('bip-0143.mediawiki', 'is the double SHA256 of the serialization of all output')) evaluates to ('01', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b1_secrecy']['sighash_byte'], L.has('core_src_script_interpreter.cpp', 'SIGHASH_NONE', 'SIGHASH_SINGLE', 'SIGHASH_ANYONECANPAY'), L.has('bip-0143.mediawiki', 'is the double SHA256 of the serialization of all output'))" ; chx:output "('01', True, True)" .
chx:X_SighashAllIsTheDefault rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SighashAllIsTheDefault .
chx:X_ReplayPaysNothing a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ReplayPaysNothing ; rdfs:label "a payment broadcast a second time"@en ; skos:definition "Sending an old payment again moves no more money: after the transaction was in a block, sendrawtransaction answered error code -27, Transaction outputs already in utxo set, testmempoolaccept said txn-already-known, the receiving wallet still held 1.5 coins before and after another block, and the same answer came after the next block, unlike a card number that can be charged again and again."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_ReplayPaysNothing a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b1_replay']; (r['sendrawtransaction']['error'], r['testmempoolaccept']['reject-reason'], r['balance_r'], r['balance_r_after'], R['b1_replay_after_block']['error']) evaluates to ('error code: -27 error message: Transaction outputs already in utxo set', 'txn-already-known', 1.5, 1.5, 'error code: -27 error message: Transaction outputs already in utxo set')"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b1_replay']; (r['sendrawtransaction']['error'], r['testmempoolaccept']['reject-reason'], r['balance_r'], r['balance_r_after'], R['b1_replay_after_block']['error'])" ; chx:output "('error code: -27 error message: Transaction outputs already in utxo set', 'txn-already-known', 1.5, 1.5, 'error code: -27 error message: Transaction outputs already in utxo set')" .
chx:X_ReplayPaysNothing rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ReplayPaysNothing .
chx:X_BookSaysNoEncryption a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BookSaysNoEncryption ; rdfs:label "a sentence of the book and a default of 2024"@en ; skos:definition "The chapter says that no encryption is required for Bitcoin traffic, and its chapter 10 says that Bitcoin Core communicates entirely in the clear at the time of writing; the release notes of 26.0 added the BIP 324 v2 transport switched off, those of 27.0 say it is now enabled by default, the help text of 31.1 says -v2transport (default: 1), and the first test node listed P2P_V2 among its services."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_BookSaysNoEncryption a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'no encryption is required for Bitcoin traffic'), L.has('core_relnotes_26.0.md', 'It is off by default'), L.has('core_relnotes_27.0.md', 'BIP324 v2 transport is now enabled by default'), L.has('book_ch10_network.adoc', 'communicates entirely in the clear, as does the modern implementation of Bitcoin Core at the time of writing'), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', '-v2transport Support v2 transport (default: 1)'), R['b2_netinfo']['P_localservices']) evaluates to (True, True, True, True, True, ['NETWORK', 'WITNESS', 'NETWORK_LIMITED', 'P2P_V2'])"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'no encryption is required for Bitcoin traffic'), L.has('core_relnotes_26.0.md', 'It is off by default'), L.has('core_relnotes_27.0.md', 'BIP324 v2 transport is now enabled by default'), L.has('book_ch10_network.adoc', 'communicates entirely in the clear, as does the modern implementation of Bitcoin Core at the time of writing'), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', '-v2transport Support v2 transport (default: 1)'), R['b2_netinfo']['P_localservices'])" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True, True, ['NETWORK', 'WITNESS', 'NETWORK_LIMITED', 'P2P_V2'])" .
chx:X_BookSaysNoEncryption rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BookSaysNoEncryption .
chx:X_V2SessionOnBothSides a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:V2SessionOnBothSides ; rdfs:label "two private nodes with one session id"@en ; skos:definition "When two Bitcoin Core 31.1 nodes connected on the loopback address, both reported the transport v2 and the same 64-hex-digit session id, the value that BIP 324 exports so that the operators of two nodes can compare it and detect a man in the middle."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_V2SessionOnBothSides a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = R['b2_peers']; (p['Q'][0]['transport'], p['P'][0]['transport'], R['b2_session_ids_match'], R['b2_session_id_len_hex'], L.has('bip-0324.mediawiki', 'session ID')) evaluates to ('v2', 'v2', True, 64, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = R['b2_peers']; (p['Q'][0]['transport'], p['P'][0]['transport'], R['b2_session_ids_match'], R['b2_session_id_len_hex'], L.has('bip-0324.mediawiki', 'session ID'))" ; chx:output "('v2', 'v2', True, 64, True)" .
chx:X_V2SessionOnBothSides rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_V2SessionOnBothSides .
chx:X_DowngradeToV1 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DowngradeToV1 ; rdfs:label "a node told to stay plain"@en ; skos:definition "Encryption is opportunistic: a node started with -v2transport=0 did not list P2P_V2 among its services, connected to the same listening node as a v1 peer with an empty session id, and so the listening node showed one v2 peer and one v1 peer at the same moment, the downgrade that BIP 324 says an attacker must perform to keep eavesdropping."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_DowngradeToV1 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = R['b2_peers']; (p['X'][0]['transport'], p['X'][0]['session_id'], [y['transport'] for y in p['P']].count('v1'), R['b2_netinfo']['X_localservices'], L.has('bip-0324.mediawiki', 'by downgrading connections to v1')) evaluates to ('v1', '', 1, ['NETWORK', 'WITNESS', 'NETWORK_LIMITED'], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); p = R['b2_peers']; (p['X'][0]['transport'], p['X'][0]['session_id'], [y['transport'] for y in p['P']].count('v1'), R['b2_netinfo']['X_localservices'], L.has('bip-0324.mediawiki', 'by downgrading connections to v1'))" ; chx:output "('v1', '', 1, ['NETWORK', 'WITNESS', 'NETWORK_LIMITED'], True)" .
chx:X_DowngradeToV1 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_DowngradeToV1 .
chx:X_GenesisHashHardCoded a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GenesisHashHardCoded ; rdfs:label "the first block, typed into the program"@en ; skos:definition "The one block a node takes without proof is typed into its source: chainparams.cpp asserts that the mainnet genesis hash is 000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f, the genesis block of the saved explorer data has exactly that id at height 0, and the regtest genesis of the test node, 0f9188f1..., with no previous block, is typed into the same file, which is the book's sentence that a validated chain uses the genesis block as its root of trust."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_GenesisHashHardCoded a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.jload('mempool_block_0.json'); q = chr(34); (g['id'], g['height'], L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'assert(consensus.hashGenesisBlock == uint256{' + q + g['id'] + q + '})'), R['b1_genesis']['previousblockhash'], R['b1_genesis']['hash'][:8], L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', R['b1_genesis']['hash']), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'genesis block as the root of trust')) evaluates to ('000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f', 0, True, None, '0f9188f1', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); g = L.jload('mempool_block_0.json'); q = chr(34); (g['id'], g['height'], L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'assert(consensus.hashGenesisBlock == uint256{' + q + g['id'] + q + '})'), R['b1_genesis']['previousblockhash'], R['b1_genesis']['hash'][:8], L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', R['b1_genesis']['hash']), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'genesis block as the root of trust'))" ; chx:output "('000000000019d6689c085ae165831e934ff763ae46a2a6c172b3f1b60a8ce26f', 0, True, None, '0f9188f1', True, True)" .
chx:X_GenesisHashHardCoded rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GenesisHashHardCoded .
chx:X_GenerateblockRefusesBadSignature a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:GenerateblockRefusesBadSignature ; rdfs:label "a block with a forged payment"@en ; skos:definition "A node validates what it is asked to mine: generateblock with the address-swapped transaction answered error code -25, TestBlockValidity failed: block-script-verify-flag-failed (Script evaluated without error but finished with a false/empty top stack element), while the same call with the correct transaction returned a block hash."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_GenerateblockRefusesBadSignature a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b1_generateblock_bad']['error'].split(', input')[0], R['b1_generateblock_good']) evaluates to ('error code: -25 error message: TestBlockValidity failed: block-script-verify-flag-failed (Script evaluated without error but finished with a false/empty top stack element)', {'ok': True})"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b1_generateblock_bad']['error'].split(', input')[0], R['b1_generateblock_good'])" ; chx:output "('error code: -25 error message: TestBlockValidity failed: block-script-verify-flag-failed (Script evaluated without error but finished with a false/empty top stack element)', {'ok': True})" .
chx:X_GenerateblockRefusesBadSignature rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_GenerateblockRefusesBadSignature .
chx:X_AssumeValidShortcut a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:AssumeValidShortcut ; rdfs:label "a trusted block that is not the genesis"@en ; skos:definition "The book says that the only thing explicitly trusted is a fully validated blockchain, but Bitcoin Core 31.1 ships a second anchor: defaultAssumeValid is block 938,343 (00000000000000000000cceb...), mined on 2026-02-25 21:32:53 UTC, 33,237 blocks below the tip of 971,580 on the day of the fetch, and the node by default assumes that block and its ancestors are valid and potentially skips their script verification, unless it is started with -assumevalid=0."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_AssumeValidShortcut a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_938343.json'); tip = int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')); q = chr(34); (b['height'], b['id'][:24], L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'consensus.defaultAssumeValid = uint256{' + q + b['id'] + q + '}; // 938343'), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'assume that it and its ancestors are valid and potentially skip their script verification'), tip - b['height'], L.iso(b['timestamp']), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'the only thing that should be explicitly trusted is a fully validated blockchain')) evaluates to (938343, '00000000000000000000cceb', True, True, 33237, '2026-02-25 21:32:53', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = L.jload('mempool_block_938343.json'); tip = int(L.raw('mempool_tip_height.txt')); q = chr(34); (b['height'], b['id'][:24], L.has('core_src_kernel_chainparams.cpp', 'consensus.defaultAssumeValid = uint256{' + q + b['id'] + q + '}; // 938343'), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', 'assume that it and its ancestors are valid and potentially skip their script verification'), tip - b['height'], L.iso(b['timestamp']), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'the only thing that should be explicitly trusted is a fully validated blockchain'))" ; chx:output "(938343, '00000000000000000000cceb', True, True, 33237, '2026-02-25 21:32:53', True)" .
chx:X_AssumeValidShortcut rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_AssumeValidShortcut .
chx:X_TarballHashMatches a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TarballHashMatches ; rdfs:label "one line of 28 in the signed list"@en ; skos:definition "The binary used for every experiment of this chapter was checked against the published list: the SHA-256 of the 90,293,352-byte tarball bitcoin-31.1-x86_64-linux-gnu.tar.gz, starting b80d9c3e04da78fb, equals its line among the 28 lines of SHA256SUMS and that line is in the saved copy of the list."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_TarballHashMatches a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b8_release']; (r['match'], r['tarball_sha256'][:16], r['tarball_bytes'], r['n_lines_in_list'], L.has('bitcoincore_31.1_SHA256SUMS.txt', r['tarball_sha256'] + '  bitcoin-31.1-x86_64-linux-gnu.tar.gz')) evaluates to (True, 'b80d9c3e04da78fb', 90293352, 28, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b8_release']; (r['match'], r['tarball_sha256'][:16], r['tarball_bytes'], r['n_lines_in_list'], L.has('bitcoincore_31.1_SHA256SUMS.txt', r['tarball_sha256'] + '  bitcoin-31.1-x86_64-linux-gnu.tar.gz'))" ; chx:output "(True, 'b80d9c3e04da78fb', 90293352, 28, True)" .
chx:X_TarballHashMatches rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TarballHashMatches .
chx:X_SignatureNeedsKeys a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SignatureNeedsKeys ; rdfs:label "a hash is not a signature"@en ; skos:definition "A matching hash proves nothing if the list itself came from the attacker: SHA256SUMS.asc holds 11 detached signatures of the builders, gpg found all 11 of them and could call none of them good with an empty keyring, exit code 2 and 11 times No public key, and the Guix instructions of Bitcoin Core say the aim is to reproduce the toolchain instead of blindly trusting binary downloads."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_SignatureNeedsKeys a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b8_release']; (r['gpg_exit'], r['gpg_has_signature_line'], r['n_signatures_made'], r['n_cannot_check_no_public_key'], L.text('bitcoincore_31.1_SHA256SUMS.asc.txt').count('BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE'), L.has('core_contrib_guix_README.md', 'our toolchain instead of blindly _trusting_ binary downloads')) evaluates to (2, False, 11, 11, 11, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); r = R['b8_release']; (r['gpg_exit'], r['gpg_has_signature_line'], r['n_signatures_made'], r['n_cannot_check_no_public_key'], L.text('bitcoincore_31.1_SHA256SUMS.asc.txt').count('BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE'), L.has('core_contrib_guix_README.md', 'our toolchain instead of blindly _trusting_ binary downloads'))" ; chx:output "(2, False, 11, 11, 11, True)" .
chx:X_SignatureNeedsKeys rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SignatureNeedsKeys .
chx:X_WatchOnlyCannotSign a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:WatchOnlyCannotSign ; rdfs:label "a wallet that only watches"@en ; skos:definition "A watch-only wallet holds public descriptors, so it can receive and build a payment but not sign: the hot node's wallet had private keys disabled, walletprocesspsbt returned complete false with no signature added, listdescriptors with private keys failed with -4 Can't get private descriptor string for watch-only wallets, and the PSBT carried the key origin data (bip32_derivs) that the signer needs."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_WatchOnlyCannotSign a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = R['b3_hot']; (h['watch_private_keys_enabled'], h['hot_sign_complete'], h['partial_sigs_before'], h['hot_sign_attempt_sigs'], h['hot_listdescriptors_private']['error'].replace(chr(39), chr(8217)), h['has_bip32_derivs']) evaluates to (False, False, [0], [0], 'error code: -4 error message: Can’t get private descriptor string for watch-only wallets', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = R['b3_hot']; (h['watch_private_keys_enabled'], h['hot_sign_complete'], h['partial_sigs_before'], h['hot_sign_attempt_sigs'], h['hot_listdescriptors_private']['error'].replace(chr(39), chr(8217)), h['has_bip32_derivs'])" ; chx:output "(False, False, [0], [0], 'error code: -4 error message: Can’t get private descriptor string for watch-only wallets', True)" .
chx:X_WatchOnlyCannotSign rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_WatchOnlyCannotSign .
chx:X_PsbtThroughColdNode a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PsbtThroughColdNode ; rdfs:label "528 characters out, 596 back"@en ; skos:definition "A cold wallet can sign without a blockchain: the cold node had 0 blocks and 0 connections, took the unsigned PSBT of 528 characters, returned a signed PSBT of 596 characters with the final witness, and the hot node finalized and broadcast it, giving 1 confirmation and 1.0 coin received, the Creator, Updater, Signer, Finalizer flow of BIP 174; a second computer is not an air gap, and Wikipedia notes that viruses such as Stuxnet were designed to infect air-gapped systems through removable media."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_PsbtThroughColdNode a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_cold']; b = R['b3_broadcast']; (c['blocks'], c['connections'], c['sign_complete'], c['final_witness_in_psbt'], R['b3_hot']['psbt_chars'], c['psbt_chars_signed'], b['finalize_complete'], b['confirmations'], b['dest_received'], L.has('bip-0174.mediawiki', 'Creator'), L.has('wikipedia_air_gap.txt', 'designed to infect air-gapped systems by exploiting security holes related to the handling of removable media')) evaluates to (0, 0, True, True, 528, 596, True, 1, 1.0, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = R['b3_cold']; b = R['b3_broadcast']; (c['blocks'], c['connections'], c['sign_complete'], c['final_witness_in_psbt'], R['b3_hot']['psbt_chars'], c['psbt_chars_signed'], b['finalize_complete'], b['confirmations'], b['dest_received'], L.has('bip-0174.mediawiki', 'Creator'), L.has('wikipedia_air_gap.txt', 'designed to infect air-gapped systems by exploiting security holes related to the handling of removable media'))" ; chx:output "(0, 0, True, True, 528, 596, True, 1, 1.0, True, True)" .
chx:X_PsbtThroughColdNode rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PsbtThroughColdNode .
chx:X_LockedWalletRefuses a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:LockedWalletRefuses ; rdfs:label "what a locked wallet will not do"@en ; skos:definition "An encrypted and locked wallet still shows its balance of 1.0 coin, hands out addresses and lists public descriptors, but sending and listing private descriptors both fail with error code -13, Please enter the wallet passphrase with walletpassphrase first, and unlocked_until reads 0."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_LockedWalletRefuses a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); l = R['b4_locked']; (l['send']['error'], l['listdescriptors_private']['error'], l['getnewaddress'], l['listdescriptors_public'], l['balance_visible'], l['unlocked_until']) evaluates to ('error code: -13 error message: Error: Please enter the wallet passphrase with walletpassphrase first.', 'error code: -13 error message: Error: Please enter the wallet passphrase with walletpassphrase first.', 'ok', 'ok', 1.0, 0)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); l = R['b4_locked']; (l['send']['error'], l['listdescriptors_private']['error'], l['getnewaddress'], l['listdescriptors_public'], l['balance_visible'], l['unlocked_until'])" ; chx:output "('error code: -13 error message: Error: Please enter the wallet passphrase with walletpassphrase first.', 'error code: -13 error message: Error: Please enter the wallet passphrase with walletpassphrase first.', 'ok', 'ok', 1.0, 0)" .
chx:X_LockedWalletRefuses rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_LockedWalletRefuses .
chx:X_WrongPassphraseError a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:WrongPassphraseError ; rdfs:label "error 14 and the passphrase that cannot be recovered"@en ; skos:definition "A wrong passphrase gives error code -14, The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect; after walletpassphrasechange the old passphrase gave -14 as well and the new one worked, and the managing-wallets document of Bitcoin Core states that there is no way to recover a passphrase."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_WrongPassphraseError a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b4_wrong']['error'], R['b4_old_passphrase']['error'], R['b4_change'], R['b4_new_passphrase'], L.has('core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'There is no way to recover a passphrase')) evaluates to ('error code: -14 error message: Error: The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.', 'error code: -14 error message: Error: The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.', {'ok': ''}, {'ok': ''}, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b4_wrong']['error'], R['b4_old_passphrase']['error'], R['b4_change'], R['b4_new_passphrase'], L.has('core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'There is no way to recover a passphrase'))" ; chx:output "('error code: -14 error message: Error: The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.', 'error code: -14 error message: Error: The wallet passphrase entered was incorrect.', {'ok': ''}, {'ok': ''}, True)" .
chx:X_WrongPassphraseError rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_WrongPassphraseError .
chx:X_UnlockTimeout a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:UnlockTimeout ; rdfs:label "three seconds of open door"@en ; skos:definition "walletpassphrase keeps the key in memory only for the timeout: unlocked_until was exactly 3 seconds ahead of now, a send in that window worked, after 5 seconds unlocked_until was 0 and the send failed with -13 again, walletlock gave 0 at once, and the timeout is capped at 100000000 seconds, about 3 years, in the source."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_UnlockTimeout a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); u = R['b4_unlocked']; (u['unlocked_until'] - u['now'], u['send_ok'], R['b4_after_timeout']['unlocked_until'], R['b4_after_timeout']['send']['error'], R['b4_walletlock_until'], L.has('core_src_wallet_rpc_encrypt.cpp', 'capped at 100000000 (~3 years)')) evaluates to (3, True, 0, 'error code: -13 error message: Error: Please enter the wallet passphrase with walletpassphrase first.', 0, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); u = R['b4_unlocked']; (u['unlocked_until'] - u['now'], u['send_ok'], R['b4_after_timeout']['unlocked_until'], R['b4_after_timeout']['send']['error'], R['b4_walletlock_until'], L.has('core_src_wallet_rpc_encrypt.cpp', 'capped at 100000000 (~3 years)'))" ; chx:output "(3, True, 0, 'error code: -13 error message: Error: Please enter the wallet passphrase with walletpassphrase first.', 0, True)" .
chx:X_UnlockTimeout rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_UnlockTimeout .
chx:X_CrypterParameters a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CrypterParameters ; rdfs:label "AES-256 and a stretch sized for 2004"@en ; skos:definition "The master key of the wallet is encrypted with AES-256-CBC under a key of 32 bytes, with a salt of 8 bytes and an IV of 16 bytes, derived by SHA-512 rounds that default to 25000, a number the source says was just under 0.1 seconds on a 1.86 GHz Pentium M, which is 12.2 times the 2048 rounds of BIP 39."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_CrypterParameters a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'WALLET_CRYPTO_KEY_SIZE'), L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'WALLET_CRYPTO_SALT_SIZE'), L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'WALLET_CRYPTO_IV_SIZE'), L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'DEFAULT_DERIVE_ITERATIONS'), L.has('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'AES-256-CBC'), L.has('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', '25000 rounds is just under 0.1 seconds on a 1.86 GHz Pentium M'), round(25000 / 2048, 1)) evaluates to ('32', '8', '16', '25000', True, True, 12.2)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'WALLET_CRYPTO_KEY_SIZE'), L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'WALLET_CRYPTO_SALT_SIZE'), L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'WALLET_CRYPTO_IV_SIZE'), L.const('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'DEFAULT_DERIVE_ITERATIONS'), L.has('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', 'AES-256-CBC'), L.has('core_src_wallet_crypter.h', '25000 rounds is just under 0.1 seconds on a 1.86 GHz Pentium M'), round(25000 / 2048, 1))" ; chx:output "('32', '8', '16', '25000', True, True, 12.2)" .
chx:X_CrypterParameters rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CrypterParameters .
chx:X_EncryptionMakesNewSeed a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:EncryptionMakesNewSeed ; rdfs:label "the backup you made yesterday is now wrong"@en ; skos:definition "Encrypting a wallet makes a new HD seed and flushes the keypool: the RPC answered wallet encrypted; The keypool has been flushed and a new HD seed was generated, the 32 bytes of the old key were in the wallet file before (True) and not after (False) in this run, the file grew from 24,576 to 36,864 bytes, and the source and the managing-wallets document both say to make a new backup at once."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_EncryptionMakesNewSeed a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b4_file']; (f['encryptwallet_message'][:60], f['master_key_bytes_in_file_before'], f['master_key_bytes_in_file_after'], f['xprv_text_in_file_before'], f['size_before'], f['size_after'], L.has('core_src_wallet_rpc_encrypt.cpp', 'the encryption process will generate a new HD seed'), L.has('core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'Any bitcoins received by the new seed cannot be recovered from the previous backups')) evaluates to ('wallet encrypted; The keypool has been flushed and a new HD ', True, False, False, 24576, 36864, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); f = R['b4_file']; (f['encryptwallet_message'][:60], f['master_key_bytes_in_file_before'], f['master_key_bytes_in_file_after'], f['xprv_text_in_file_before'], f['size_before'], f['size_after'], L.has('core_src_wallet_rpc_encrypt.cpp', 'the encryption process will generate a new HD seed'), L.has('core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'Any bitcoins received by the new seed cannot be recovered from the previous backups'))" ; chx:output "('wallet encrypted; The keypool has been flushed and a new HD ', True, False, False, 24576, 36864, True, True)" .
chx:X_EncryptionMakesNewSeed rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_EncryptionMakesNewSeed .
chx:X_ExternalSignerSupport a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ExternalSignerSupport ; rdfs:label "a node that asks a device to sign"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Core can be started with -signer=<cmd> so that an external tool, for example HWI, signs for a hardware device; the Bitcoin Wiki says the keys are generated by the device and never leave it, and the book says a signing device only needs to hold keys and use them to generate signatures."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_ExternalSignerSupport a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_doc_external-signer.md', 'Bitcoin Core can be launched with `-signer=<cmd>`'), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', '-signer=<cmd>'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_hardware_wallet.txt', 'private keys are generated by the device and never leave it'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'a Bitcoin hardware signing device only needs to hold keys and use them to generate signatures')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('core_doc_external-signer.md', 'Bitcoin Core can be launched with `-signer=<cmd>`'), L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', '-signer=<cmd>'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_hardware_wallet.txt', 'private keys are generated by the device and never leave it'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'a Bitcoin hardware signing device only needs to hold keys and use them to generate signatures'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_ExternalSignerSupport rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ExternalSignerSupport .
chx:X_HardwareDoesNotCheckTheAddress a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HardwareDoesNotCheckTheAddress ; rdfs:label "malware swaps the recipient"@en ; skos:definition "A hardware wallet protects the key and not the intention: the Bitcoin Wiki warns that malware on a PC could monitor for high-value transactions and swap out the recipient's address, so the person must read the address on the device's own screen, and the same page lists Trezor first among the commercial hardware wallets, in chronological order."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_HardwareDoesNotCheckTheAddress a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_hardware_wallet.txt', 'malware on a PC could monitor for high value transactions and then swap out the recipient'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_hardware_wallet.txt', 'Commercial hardware wallets (ordered chronologically) 3.1 Trezor')) evaluates to (True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_hardware_wallet.txt', 'malware on a PC could monitor for high value transactions and then swap out the recipient'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_hardware_wallet.txt', 'Commercial hardware wallets (ordered chronologically) 3.1 Trezor'))" ; chx:output "(True, True)" .
chx:X_HardwareDoesNotCheckTheAddress rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HardwareDoesNotCheckTheAddress .
chx:X_TrezorPinWait a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TrezorPinWait ; rdfs:label "9 hours of waiting before the wipe"@en ; skos:definition "The PIN of a Trezor is protected by doubling waits, 1, 2, 4 seconds and so on, and a wipe after 16 failed attempts, so the waits before the sixteenth attempt add up to 32,767 seconds, 9.1 hours, a rule that makes guessing slow and finite."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_TrezorPinWait a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); w = [2 ** k for k in range(15)]; (sum(w), round(sum(w) / 3600, 1), L.has('bitcoinwiki_trezor.txt', 'The device automatically wipe itself after 16 failed PIN entry attempts'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_trezor.txt', '1 second after the first attempt, 2 seconds after the second attempt, and 4 seconds after the third attempt')) evaluates to (32767, 9.1, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); w = [2 ** k for k in range(15)]; (sum(w), round(sum(w) / 3600, 1), L.has('bitcoinwiki_trezor.txt', 'The device automatically wipe itself after 16 failed PIN entry attempts'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_trezor.txt', '1 second after the first attempt, 2 seconds after the second attempt, and 4 seconds after the third attempt'))" ; chx:output "(32767, 9.1, True, True)" .
chx:X_TrezorPinWait rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TrezorPinWait .
chx:X_PaperWalletsAreObsolete a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:PaperWalletsAreObsolete ; rdfs:label "a printed key that the printer remembers"@en ; skos:definition "The book recommends a seed printed on paper as a backup, but the Bitcoin Wiki now calls the paper wallet an obsolete and unsafe method that was popular between 2011 and 2016, because printers often have a hard drive that keeps the file; the distinction is a single private key on paper against a seed on paper."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_PaperWalletsAreObsolete a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_paper_wallet.txt', 'obsolete and unsafe method of storing bitcoin which was popular between 2011 and 2016'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_paper_wallet.txt', 'Many printers have a hard drive for internal storage'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'is printed on paper is called a')) evaluates to (True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_paper_wallet.txt', 'obsolete and unsafe method of storing bitcoin which was popular between 2011 and 2016'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_paper_wallet.txt', 'Many printers have a hard drive for internal storage'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'is printed on paper is called a'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True)" .
chx:X_PaperWalletsAreObsolete rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_PaperWalletsAreObsolete .
chx:X_BrainwalletCrackTime a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BrainwalletCrackTime ; rdfs:label "four words that fall in 18 seconds"@en ; skos:definition "A secret made of four words chosen from a list of 2,048 has 2 to the power 44 possibilities, which a machine trying a trillion guesses per second (an assumed rate, not a measurement) exhausts in 17.6 seconds, while 128 bits are 2 to the power 84 times more, which is why a brainwallet from a memorized phrase is attacked with dictionaries and a seed is generated at random."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_BrainwalletCrackTime a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = 2048 ** 4; (n == 2 ** 44, round(n / 1e12, 1), len(L.wordlist()), 2 ** 128 // n == 2 ** 84, L.has('bitcoinwiki_brainwallet.txt', 'can be tested with dictionary attacks')) evaluates to (True, 17.6, 2048, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = 2048 ** 4; (n == 2 ** 44, round(n / 1e12, 1), len(L.wordlist()), 2 ** 128 // n == 2 ** 84, L.has('bitcoinwiki_brainwallet.txt', 'can be tested with dictionary attacks'))" ; chx:output "(True, 17.6, 2048, True, True)" .
chx:X_BrainwalletCrackTime rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BrainwalletCrackTime .
chx:X_Bip39MnemonicChecksum a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip39MnemonicChecksum ; rdfs:label "twelve words and four spare bits"@en ; skos:definition "A BIP 39 phrase of 12 words is 132 bits, 128 of entropy and 4 of checksum: the 16 zero bytes of the first test vector give abandon eleven times and about, the library reproduces that exactly, the list has 2,048 words, and replacing the last word by zoo or abandon makes the phrase invalid."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_Bip39MnemonicChecksum a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = L.jload('bip39_trezor_vectors.json')['english'][0]; m = L.bip39_mnemonic(bytes.fromhex(v[0])); w = m.split(); (m == v[1], len(w), len(L.wordlist()), L.bip39_valid(m), L.bip39_valid(' '.join(w[:-1] + ['zoo'])), L.bip39_valid(' '.join(w[:-1] + ['abandon'])), 12 * 11 - 128) evaluates to (True, 12, 2048, True, False, False, 4)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = L.jload('bip39_trezor_vectors.json')['english'][0]; m = L.bip39_mnemonic(bytes.fromhex(v[0])); w = m.split(); (m == v[1], len(w), len(L.wordlist()), L.bip39_valid(m), L.bip39_valid(' '.join(w[:-1] + ['zoo'])), L.bip39_valid(' '.join(w[:-1] + ['abandon'])), 12 * 11 - 128)" ; chx:output "(True, 12, 2048, True, False, False, 4)" .
chx:X_Bip39MnemonicChecksum rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip39MnemonicChecksum .
chx:X_Bip39SeedFromWords a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip39SeedFromWords ; rdfs:label "2048 rounds from words to a seed"@en ; skos:definition "The seed is PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA512 and 2048 rounds over the words, with the salt mnemonic plus the optional passphrase: with the passphrase TREZOR the library reproduced the 64-byte seed and the master xprv of the Trezor test vector, and without the passphrase the seed begins 5eb00bbddcf06908, a completely different wallet."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_Bip39SeedFromWords a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = L.jload('bip39_trezor_vectors.json')['english'][0]; s = L.bip39_seed(v[1], 'TREZOR'); (s.hex() == v[2], L.bip39_seed(v[1]).hex()[:16], L.bip32_master(s)[0] == v[3], L.has('bip-0039.mediawiki', 'The iteration count is set to 2048 and HMAC-SHA512 is used as the pseudo-random function')) evaluates to (True, '5eb00bbddcf06908', True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); v = L.jload('bip39_trezor_vectors.json')['english'][0]; s = L.bip39_seed(v[1], 'TREZOR'); (s.hex() == v[2], L.bip39_seed(v[1]).hex()[:16], L.bip32_master(s)[0] == v[3], L.has('bip-0039.mediawiki', 'The iteration count is set to 2048 and HMAC-SHA512 is used as the pseudo-random function'))" ; chx:output "(True, '5eb00bbddcf06908', True, True)" .
chx:X_Bip39SeedFromWords rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip39SeedFromWords .
chx:X_Bip32MasterVector a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Bip32MasterVector ; rdfs:label "the master key of test vector 1"@en ; skos:definition "From the seed 000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f the master key is HMAC-SHA512 keyed with the text Bitcoin seed, the left 32 bytes (starting e8f32e723decf405) are the private key and the right 32 bytes the chain code, and the Base58Check form xprv9s21ZrQH143K3QTDL4LXw2F7HEK3wJUD2nW2nRk4stbPy6cq3jPPqjiChkVvvNKmPGJxWUtg6LnF5kejMRNNU3TGtRBeJgk33yuGBxrMPHi is the one printed in BIP 32."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_Bip32MasterVector a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = L.bip32_master(bytes.fromhex('000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f')); (m[0], L.has('bip-0032.mediawiki', m[0]), m[1][:16], len(m[2]) // 2) evaluates to ('xprv9s21ZrQH143K3QTDL4LXw2F7HEK3wJUD2nW2nRk4stbPy6cq3jPPqjiChkVvvNKmPGJxWUtg6LnF5kejMRNNU3TGtRBeJgk33yuGBxrMPHi', True, 'e8f32e723decf405', 32)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); m = L.bip32_master(bytes.fromhex('000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f')); (m[0], L.has('bip-0032.mediawiki', m[0]), m[1][:16], len(m[2]) // 2)" ; chx:output "('xprv9s21ZrQH143K3QTDL4LXw2F7HEK3wJUD2nW2nRk4stbPy6cq3jPPqjiChkVvvNKmPGJxWUtg6LnF5kejMRNNU3TGtRBeJgk33yuGBxrMPHi', True, 'e8f32e723decf405', 32)" .
chx:X_Bip32MasterVector rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Bip32MasterVector .
chx:X_CoreHasNoMnemonics a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CoreHasNoMnemonics ; rdfs:label "Core keeps a wallet file, not twelve words"@en ; skos:definition "Bitcoin Core does not use BIP 39 words: none of seven saved Core files (the backup, wallet and encrypt RPC sources, the managing-wallets, descriptors and PSBT documents and the command line help) mentions a mnemonic or BIP 39, while the book's chapter 5 does mention SLIP39, so recovery in Core is by backupwallet files and descriptors."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_CoreHasNoMnemonics a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([f for f in ('core_src_wallet_rpc_backup.cpp', 'core_src_wallet_rpc_wallet.cpp', 'core_src_wallet_rpc_encrypt.cpp', 'core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'core_doc_descriptors.md', 'core_doc_psbt.md', 'bitcoind_help_31.1.txt') if L.has(f, 'mnemonic') or L.has(f, 'BIP39') or L.has(f, 'BIP 39 ') or L.has(f, 'BIP-39')], L.has('book_ch05_wallets.adoc', 'SLIP39')) evaluates to ([], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); ([f for f in ('core_src_wallet_rpc_backup.cpp', 'core_src_wallet_rpc_wallet.cpp', 'core_src_wallet_rpc_encrypt.cpp', 'core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'core_doc_descriptors.md', 'core_doc_psbt.md', 'bitcoind_help_31.1.txt') if L.has(f, 'mnemonic') or L.has(f, 'BIP39') or L.has(f, 'BIP 39 ') or L.has(f, 'BIP-39')], L.has('book_ch05_wallets.adoc', 'SLIP39'))" ; chx:output "([], True)" .
chx:X_CoreHasNoMnemonics rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CoreHasNoMnemonics .
chx:X_RestoreGivesSameAddresses a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:RestoreGivesSameAddresses ; rdfs:label "a backup file that restores the lot"@en ; skos:definition "A file made by backupwallet and restored by restorewallet gave the same wallet: the source wallet and the restored one both held 3.0 coins, the next new address of the restored wallet was the address the source handed out next, and the address far along the chain belonged to it."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_RestoreGivesSameAddresses a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b5_backup']; (b['balance_src'], b['balance_fresh'], b['fresh_next_matches'], b['far_address_ismine_fresh'], b['restore_fresh'], L.has('core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'restorewallet')) evaluates to (3.0, 3.0, True, True, {'name': 'from_fresh'}, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b5_backup']; (b['balance_src'], b['balance_fresh'], b['fresh_next_matches'], b['far_address_ismine_fresh'], b['restore_fresh'], L.has('core_doc_managing-wallets.md', 'restorewallet'))" ; chx:output "(3.0, 3.0, True, True, {'name': 'from_fresh'}, True)" .
chx:X_RestoreGivesSameAddresses rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_RestoreGivesSameAddresses .
chx:X_StaleBackupMissesFunds a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:StaleBackupMissesFunds ; rdfs:label "coins sent to the tenth address"@en ; skos:definition "A backup does not know what happens after it: on a node with -keypool=3 the stale copy restored 1.0 coin of the 3.0, because the later 2.0 coins went to the tenth address, outside the stale range 0 to 2, while the help text of the option warns that smaller sizes may increase the risk of losing funds when restoring from an old backup; the default size is 1000."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_StaleBackupMissesFunds a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b5_backup']; (b['keypool_range_end'], b['far_index'], b['balance_src'], b['balance_stale'], b['far_address_ismine_stale'], b['stale_first_next_equals_src_second'], L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', '-keypool=<n> Set key pool size to <n> (default: 1000). Warning: Smaller sizes may increase the risk of losing funds when restoring from an old backup')) evaluates to ([0, 2], 9, 3.0, 1.0, False, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b5_backup']; (b['keypool_range_end'], b['far_index'], b['balance_src'], b['balance_stale'], b['far_address_ismine_stale'], b['stale_first_next_equals_src_second'], L.has('bitcoind_help_31.1.txt', '-keypool=<n> Set key pool size to <n> (default: 1000). Warning: Smaller sizes may increase the risk of losing funds when restoring from an old backup'))" ; chx:output "([0, 2], 9, 3.0, 1.0, False, True, True)" .
chx:X_StaleBackupMissesFunds rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_StaleBackupMissesFunds .
chx:X_DescriptorIsPartOfBackup a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:DescriptorIsPartOfBackup ; rdfs:label "three keys are not an address"@en ; skos:definition "The book's warning about backing up more than the seed is true in the node: a wallet that held one of the three keys had no idea of the multisig address (balance 0.0), a wallet given the full descriptor again found the 2.0 coins, and the same three keys in a different order under multi gave another address and balance 0.0."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_DescriptorIsPartOfBackup a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b6_backup']; o = R['b6_order']; (b['m1_knows_multisig_address'], b['m1_balance'], b['ms_balance'], b['rebuilt_balance'], b['wrongorder_balance'], o['multi_same'], L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'Wallet recovery codes must include this information')) evaluates to (False, 2.0, 2.0, 2.0, 0.0, False, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); b = R['b6_backup']; o = R['b6_order']; (b['m1_knows_multisig_address'], b['m1_balance'], b['ms_balance'], b['rebuilt_balance'], b['wrongorder_balance'], o['multi_same'], L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'Wallet recovery codes must include this information'))" ; chx:output "(False, 2.0, 2.0, 2.0, 0.0, False, True)" .
chx:X_DescriptorIsPartOfBackup rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_DescriptorIsPartOfBackup .
chx:X_LostSevenThousand a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:LostSevenThousand ; rdfs:label "the education project that lost its keys"@en ; skos:definition "The book says that in July 2011 a well-known Bitcoin awareness and education project lost almost 7,000 bitcoin by losing the encryption keys of its backups; of the 77 saved sources only the book contains that sentence, so the event and the project are unconfirmed here and the lesson, not the name, is what the chapter can support."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_LostSevenThousand a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'In July 2011'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'almost 7,000 bitcoin'), L.count_sources_with('almost 7,000 bitcoin'), L.count_sources_with('7,000 bitcoin')) evaluates to (True, True, 1, 1)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'In July 2011'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'almost 7,000 bitcoin'), L.count_sources_with('almost 7,000 bitcoin'), L.count_sources_with('7,000 bitcoin'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, 1, 1)" .
chx:X_LostSevenThousand rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_LostSevenThousand .
chx:X_TwoOfThreeSigning a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:TwoOfThreeSigning ; rdfs:label "two pens out of three"@en ; skos:definition "A 2-of-3 wallet needs two signers: the first key alone left the PSBT incomplete with 1 signature, the first and third together made it complete, it was finalized, accepted by the mempool, and the input had four witness items (an empty dummy, two signatures and the script) in 146 virtual bytes."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_TwoOfThreeSigning a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b6_sign']; (s['m1_alone'], s['m1_m3'], s['finalize_complete'], s['accept'], s['witness_items'], s['vsize']) evaluates to ({'complete': False, 'sigs': [1]}, {'complete': True, 'sigs': [0]}, True, True, 4, 146)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s = R['b6_sign']; (s['m1_alone'], s['m1_m3'], s['finalize_complete'], s['accept'], s['witness_items'], s['vsize'])" ; chx:output "({'complete': False, 'sigs': [1]}, {'complete': True, 'sigs': [0]}, True, True, 4, 146)" .
chx:X_TwoOfThreeSigning rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_TwoOfThreeSigning .
chx:X_SortedmultiOrder a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:SortedmultiOrder ; rdfs:label "the same address from any order"@en ; skos:definition "The order of the keys in sortedmulti does not matter: the three public keys in two orders gave the same address, while multi with the same keys in two orders gave different addresses, the wallet's first address was the derived address 0, and BIP 67 says to sort the keys lexicographically by their binary form."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_SortedmultiOrder a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); o = R['b6_order']; (o['sortedmulti_same'], o['multi_same'], o['wallet_address_is_derived_0'], o['n_keys_in_descriptor'], o['descriptor_chars'], L.has('bip-0067.mediawiki', 'Sort them lexicographically according to their binary representation'), L.has('core_src_script_descriptor.cpp', 'sortedmulti')) evaluates to (True, False, True, 3, 436, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); o = R['b6_order']; (o['sortedmulti_same'], o['multi_same'], o['wallet_address_is_derived_0'], o['n_keys_in_descriptor'], o['descriptor_chars'], L.has('bip-0067.mediawiki', 'Sort them lexicographically according to their binary representation'), L.has('core_src_script_descriptor.cpp', 'sortedmulti'))" ; chx:output "(True, False, True, 3, 436, True, True)" .
chx:X_SortedmultiOrder rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_SortedmultiOrder .
chx:X_KeyLossTolerance a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:KeyLossTolerance ; rdfs:label "losing one key, losing two"@en ; skos:definition "With one of three keys lost, the other two still signed the PSBT to completion; with two lost, the remaining key left one signature and no complete transaction, which is the redundancy the book mentions for a person who keeps several keys in different places."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_KeyLossTolerance a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); l = R['b6_loss']; (l['lose_m1_sign_with_m2_m3'], l['lose_m2_m3_sign_with_m1'], l['sigs_m1_only'], L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'Multisignature addresses can also offer redundancy')) evaluates to (True, False, [1], True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); l = R['b6_loss']; (l['lose_m1_sign_with_m2_m3'], l['lose_m2_m3_sign_with_m1'], l['sigs_m1_only'], L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'Multisignature addresses can also offer redundancy'))" ; chx:output "(True, False, [1], True)" .
chx:X_KeyLossTolerance rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_KeyLossTolerance .
chx:X_OddsOfLossAndTheft a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:OddsOfLossAndTheft ; rdfs:label "a 10% chance of losing, a 5% chance of theft"@en ; skos:definition "If each key is lost with probability 0.1 and stolen with 0.05, independently (an assumption), one key alone is lost with 0.1 and stolen with 0.05; 2-of-3 is stuck with 0.028 and robbed with 0.00725; 1-of-3 is stuck with 0.001 but robbed with 0.14263; and at a loss chance of 0.5 the 2-of-3 stands exactly where the single key does, 0.5."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_OddsOfLossAndTheft a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (round(L.p_lose(0.1, 1, 1), 4), round(L.p_lose(0.1, 2, 3), 4), round(L.p_lose(0.1, 1, 3), 4), round(L.p_theft(0.05, 1, 1), 5), round(L.p_theft(0.05, 2, 3), 5), round(L.p_theft(0.05, 1, 3), 5), round(L.p_lose(0.5, 2, 3), 4)) evaluates to (0.1, 0.028, 0.001, 0.05, 0.00725, 0.14263, 0.5)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (round(L.p_lose(0.1, 1, 1), 4), round(L.p_lose(0.1, 2, 3), 4), round(L.p_lose(0.1, 1, 3), 4), round(L.p_theft(0.05, 1, 1), 5), round(L.p_theft(0.05, 2, 3), 5), round(L.p_theft(0.05, 1, 3), 5), round(L.p_lose(0.5, 2, 3), 4))" ; chx:output "(0.1, 0.028, 0.001, 0.05, 0.00725, 0.14263, 0.5)" .
chx:X_OddsOfLossAndTheft rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_OddsOfLossAndTheft .
chx:X_MultisigCostsBytes a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MultisigCostsBytes ; rdfs:label "36 more virtual bytes for the same payment"@en ; skos:definition "Safety has a price in bytes: the same one-input one-output payment took 110 virtual bytes from a single key and 146 from the 2-of-3 script, 36 more, a ratio of 1.33, which at 10 satoshis per virtual byte is 360 satoshis more."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_MultisigCostsBytes a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s, m = R['b6_single_vsize'], R['b6_sign']['vsize']; (s, m, m - s, round(m / s, 2), (m - s) * 10) evaluates to (110, 146, 36, 1.33, 360)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); s, m = R['b6_single_vsize'], R['b6_sign']['vsize']; (s, m, m - s, round(m / s, 2), (m - s) * 10)" ; chx:output "(110, 146, 36, 1.33, 360)" .
chx:X_MultisigCostsBytes rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MultisigCostsBytes .
chx:X_ShamirTwoOfThree a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:ShamirTwoOfThree ; rdfs:label "three shares, any two will do"@en ; skos:definition "Adi Shamir's scheme hides a secret as the constant term of a random polynomial: with a degree-1 polynomial over the prime 2 to the 127 minus 1, the secret 123456789 and the slope 987654321 gave the shares 1111111110, 2098765431 and 3086419752, any two of them recovered the secret, and one share did not."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_ShamirTwoOfThree a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); sh = L.shamir_split(123456789, 2, 3, [987654321]); (sh, [L.shamir_recover(c) for c in (sh[:2], sh[1:], [sh[0], sh[2]])], L.shamir_recover(sh[:1]) == 123456789, L.has('shamir_1979_how_to_share_a_secret.txt', 'Such a scheme is called a (k, n) threshold scheme')) evaluates to ([(1, 1111111110), (2, 2098765431), (3, 3086419752)], [123456789, 123456789, 123456789], False, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); sh = L.shamir_split(123456789, 2, 3, [987654321]); (sh, [L.shamir_recover(c) for c in (sh[:2], sh[1:], [sh[0], sh[2]])], L.shamir_recover(sh[:1]) == 123456789, L.has('shamir_1979_how_to_share_a_secret.txt', 'Such a scheme is called a (k, n) threshold scheme'))" ; chx:output "([(1, 1111111110), (2, 2098765431), (3, 3086419752)], [123456789, 123456789, 123456789], False, True)" .
chx:X_ShamirTwoOfThree rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_ShamirTwoOfThree .
chx:X_OneShareRevealsNothing a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:OneShareRevealsNothing ; rdfs:label "every secret remains possible"@en ; skos:definition "A single share leaves the secret completely undetermined: over the small prime 257 the share (1, 100) fits 257 pairs of secret and slope, one for each of the 257 possible secrets and 257 different slopes, which is Shamir's condition that any k minus 1 pieces leave the data completely undetermined."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_OneShareRevealsNothing a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = L.shamir_candidates((1, 100)); (len(c), len({s for s, _ in c}), len({sl for _, sl in c}), L.has('shamir_1979_how_to_share_a_secret.txt', 'leaves D completely undetermined')) evaluates to (257, 257, 257, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); c = L.shamir_candidates((1, 100)); (len(c), len({s for s, _ in c}), len({sl for _, sl in c}), L.has('shamir_1979_how_to_share_a_secret.txt', 'leaves D completely undetermined'))" ; chx:output "(257, 257, 257, True)" .
chx:X_OneShareRevealsNothing rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_OneShareRevealsNothing .
chx:X_Codex32AndSlip39 a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:Codex32AndSlip39 ; rdfs:label "the shares the chapter does not mention"@en ; skos:definition "The chapter names multisignature but never secret sharing: BIP 93 (codex32, status Draft) splits a BIP 32 seed into up to 31 shares, the book's chapter 5 lists SLIP39 as a successor to BIP39, and the word Shamir does not occur in chapter 13."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_Codex32AndSlip39 a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0093.mediawiki', 'split into up to 31 shares'), L.has('bip-0093.mediawiki', 'Status: Draft'), L.has('book_ch05_wallets.adoc', 'SLIP39'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'multisignature'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'Shamir')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True, False)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bip-0093.mediawiki', 'split into up to 31 shares'), L.has('bip-0093.mediawiki', 'Status: Draft'), L.has('book_ch05_wallets.adoc', 'SLIP39'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'multisignature'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'Shamir'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True, False)" .
chx:X_Codex32AndSlip39 rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_Codex32AndSlip39 .
chx:X_MtGoxLoss a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:MtGoxLoss ; rdfs:label "a hot wallet that held a country's worth"@en ; skos:definition "Mt. Gox, based in Shibuya, Tokyo, handled over 70% of all bitcoin transactions by early 2014 and closed after losing 744,408 bitcoins in a theft that went undetected for years (the Bitcoin Wiki says 640 thousand were lost); its loss of 850,000 fell to 650,000 when 199,999.99 were found in an old wallet, in June 2011 fraudulent trades had pushed its price down to one cent, and the Wikipedia article names its hot wallet, which fits the book's warning about exchanges that concentrate user funds in a single hot wallet on one server."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_MtGoxLoss a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_mt_gox.txt', 'handling over 70% of all bitcoin transactions worldwide by early 2014'), L.has('wikipedia_mt_gox.txt', 'lost 744,408 bitcoins in a theft which went undetected for years'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_mt_gox.txt', 'after losing 640 thousand bitcoins'), round(850000 - 199999.99, 2), L.has('wikipedia_mt_gox.txt', 'a stream of fraudulent trades caused the nominal price of a bitcoin to fraudulently drop to one cent'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'many early Bitcoin exchanges concentrated all user funds in')) evaluates to (True, True, True, 650000.01, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_mt_gox.txt', 'handling over 70% of all bitcoin transactions worldwide by early 2014'), L.has('wikipedia_mt_gox.txt', 'lost 744,408 bitcoins in a theft which went undetected for years'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_mt_gox.txt', 'after losing 640 thousand bitcoins'), round(850000 - 199999.99, 2), L.has('wikipedia_mt_gox.txt', 'a stream of fraudulent trades caused the nominal price of a bitcoin to fraudulently drop to one cent'), L.has('book_ch13_security.adoc', 'many early Bitcoin exchanges concentrated all user funds in'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, 650000.01, True, True)" .
chx:X_MtGoxLoss rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_MtGoxLoss .
chx:X_BitfinexSegregatedWallets a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:BitfinexSegregatedWallets ; rdfs:label "segregated, and still 119,756 gone"@en ; skos:definition "Bitfinex announced a hack in August 2016 in which 119,756 bitcoin were stolen from users' segregated wallets, after it had partnered with BitGo in 2015 for secured wallets, and the trading price fell by 20%, which shows that a custodian's wallet design can fail even when it is advertised as secured."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_BitfinexSegregatedWallets a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', '119,756 units of bitcoin'), L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', 'partnered with Palo Alto company BitGo'), L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', 'The bitcoin was taken from users'), L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', 'plunged by 20%')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', '119,756 units of bitcoin'), L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', 'partnered with Palo Alto company BitGo'), L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', 'The bitcoin was taken from users'), L.has('wikipedia_bitfinex.txt', 'plunged by 20%'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_BitfinexSegregatedWallets rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_BitfinexSegregatedWallets .
chx:X_CasasciusHologram a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:CasasciusHologram ; rdfs:label "a coin with a secret under a sticker"@en ; skos:definition "Casascius coins were metal coins with a private key on paper under a tamper-evident hologram, sold until 26 November 2013 in 1, 10, 25, 100 and 1000 BTC sizes; reading the key without destroying the hologram was difficult or impossible, and FinCEN told the maker that minting physical bitcoins made him a money transmitter, which ended the sales."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_CasasciusHologram a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'sold until Nov 26, 2013'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'Casascius coins are available in 1, 10, 25, 100, and 1000 BTC increments'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'minting physical bitcoins qualifies him as a money transmitter business'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'It is difficult or impossible to read the private key on the coin without damaging or destroying the hologram')) evaluates to (True, True, True, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'sold until Nov 26, 2013'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'Casascius coins are available in 1, 10, 25, 100, and 1000 BTC increments'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'minting physical bitcoins qualifies him as a money transmitter business'), L.has('bitcoinwiki_casascius.txt', 'It is difficult or impossible to read the private key on the coin without damaging or destroying the hologram'))" ; chx:output "(True, True, True, True)" .
chx:X_CasasciusHologram rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_CasasciusHologram .
chx:X_HeirWaitsTenBlocks a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:HeirWaitsTenBlocks ; rdfs:label "a key for the family that works later"@en ; skos:definition "A script can give an heir a delayed path: with or(owner, and(heir, older 10)) the owner's spend was accepted at once, the heir's spend with sequence 10 was refused as non-BIP68-final at 1 and at 9 confirmations and accepted at 10, and the heir without the sequence set could not even finish signing."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_HeirWaitsTenBlocks a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = R['b7_heir']; (R['b7_owner']['allowed'], h['sequence'], h['at_1_conf'], h['at_9_conf'], h['at_10_conf'], h['without_sequence_set']['complete'], R['b7_descriptor']['policy'], L.has('bip-0112.mediawiki', 'CHECKSEQUENCEVERIFY')) evaluates to (True, 10, {'allowed': False, 'reject_reason': 'non-BIP68-final'}, {'allowed': False, 'confirmations': 9, 'reject_reason': 'non-BIP68-final'}, {'allowed': True, 'confirmations': 10, 'reject_reason': None}, False, 'or(owner, and(heir, older 10))', True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); h = R['b7_heir']; (R['b7_owner']['allowed'], h['sequence'], h['at_1_conf'], h['at_9_conf'], h['at_10_conf'], h['without_sequence_set']['complete'], R['b7_descriptor']['policy'], L.has('bip-0112.mediawiki', 'CHECKSEQUENCEVERIFY'))" ; chx:output "(True, 10, {'allowed': False, 'reject_reason': 'non-BIP68-final'}, {'allowed': False, 'confirmations': 9, 'reject_reason': 'non-BIP68-final'}, {'allowed': True, 'confirmations': 10, 'reject_reason': None}, False, 'or(owner, and(heir, older 10))', True)" .
chx:X_HeirWaitsTenBlocks rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_HeirWaitsTenBlocks .
chx:X_OlderSixtyFiveThousand a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:OlderSixtyFiveThousand ; rdfs:label "a timelock that quietly means zero"@en ; skos:definition "BIP 68 reads only the low 16 bits of the sequence, so a wait is at most 65,535 blocks (about 455.1 days) or 65,535 units of 512 seconds (33,553,920 seconds, 388.4 days), and the descriptor parser of Bitcoin Core 31.1 accepted both older(65535) and older(65536), but the heir whose key was behind older(65536) could spend with 1 confirmation, because 65536 has no low 16 bits."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_OlderSixtyFiveThousand a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b7_limits']['65535'], R['b7_limits']['65536'], R['b7_older_65536']['allowed'], R['b7_older_65536']['confirmations'], round(65535 * 10 / 1440, 1), R['b7_unit_seconds_x65535'], round(R['b7_unit_seconds_x65535'] / 86400, 1), L.has('bip-0068.mediawiki', 'a mask of 0x0000ffff MUST be applied to the sequence field')) evaluates to ({'ok': True}, {'ok': True}, True, 1, 455.1, 33553920, 388.4, True)"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); (R['b7_limits']['65535'], R['b7_limits']['65536'], R['b7_older_65536']['allowed'], R['b7_older_65536']['confirmations'], round(65535 * 10 / 1440, 1), R['b7_unit_seconds_x65535'], round(R['b7_unit_seconds_x65535'] / 86400, 1), L.has('bip-0068.mediawiki', 'a mask of 0x0000ffff MUST be applied to the sequence field'))" ; chx:output "({'ok': True}, {'ok': True}, True, 1, 455.1, 33553920, 388.4, True)" .
chx:X_OlderSixtyFiveThousand rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_OlderSixtyFiveThousand .
chx:X_WhatWasNotExecuted a owl:NamedIndividual, chx:WhatWasNotExecuted ; rdfs:label "ten things that were not run"@en ; skos:definition "The record lists ten things that were not run in this chapter: the hardware device, a true air gap, paper and metal backups, an exchange breach, estate planning with a lawyer, mainnet funds, Shamir in a wallet, BIP 39 recovery in Core, a good gpg verification and BIP 324 on the wire, each with its reason."@en ; dcterms:source <http://example.org/sen0401/ch13/research> .
chx:IO_WhatWasNotExecuted a owl:NamedIndividual, rd:IOExample ; rdfs:label "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = R['not_executed']; (len(n), sorted(n)) evaluates to (10, ['bip324_on_the_wire', 'bip39_recovery_in_core', 'estate_planning_with_a_lawyer', 'exchange_hack_or_hot_wallet_breach', 'gpg_signature_check', 'hardware_signing_device', 'mainnet_funds', 'paper_and_metal_backups', 'shamir_slip39_in_a_wallet', 'true_air_gap'])"@en ; chx:input "import sys, math, hashlib, datetime; sys.path.insert(0, '08-tooling'); import sen0401_ch13_lib_v1_0_0 as L; R = L.run(); n = R['not_executed']; (len(n), sorted(n))" ; chx:output "(10, ['bip324_on_the_wire', 'bip39_recovery_in_core', 'estate_planning_with_a_lawyer', 'exchange_hack_or_hot_wallet_breach', 'gpg_signature_check', 'hardware_signing_device', 'mainnet_funds', 'paper_and_metal_backups', 'shamir_slip39_in_a_wallet', 'true_air_gap'])" .
chx:X_WhatWasNotExecuted rd:hasIOExample chx:IO_WhatWasNotExecuted .
